QUEST Hunt One
  title: The Truth Scavenger Hunt · Round 1
  from: Trabolta
  text:
    There are files scattered around the computer that I need your help to
    interpret. The facts are obscure. They are in the books in the Desktop.
    Fifteen minutes.
    - Q1. According to Funk and Wagnalls, what is an example of fraud?
    - Q2. According to Forensics For Dummies, finish this sentence: “___ ___ ___ ___ ___ previously hypnotized witnesses.”
    - Q3. According to Macs for Dummies, finish this sentence: “A similar online _, called pharming, also involves the use of __ ___ __.”

QUEST Hunt Two
  title: The Truth Scavenger Hunt · Round 2
  from: Trabolta
  text:
    It is more important than ever that I get the information I need. One
    hour. The books have not moved. Return to the Desktop for the Second
    Moment of Truth.
    - Q1. What is an example of a Strong Password, cited by a For Dummies book, that starts with Q?
    - Q2. What, according to one book, is the traditional objection to romance?
    - Q3. According to one encyclopedia, what trend in technological progress will lead to this outcome: “Increased wages and shorter hours will provide the leisure necessary for man’s full cultural development.”

QUEST The Final Facts
  title: The Final Fact-Finding Round
  from: Trabolta
  text:
    The last three facts. Everything depends on these facts.
    - Q1. Who is Binary Tom?
    - Q2. What is the unlikely condition that will enable you to find your child on a map using Windows 10?
